eturn is_balanced and (current_weight <= w)", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/77": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/77", "solution": "def iscube(a):\n    '''\n    Checks if an integer `a` is a perfect cube of some integer.\n    Handles positive, negative, and zero inputs.\n    '''\n    \n    original_a = a\n\n    # Determine the sign of the number; cube root of negative numbers is negative.\n    sign = 1\n    if a < 0:\n        sign = -1\n        a = -a # Work with the absolute value for the power operation\n\n    # Calculate the approximate cube root of the positive number using floating point.\n    # round() will find the nearest integer.\n    root = round(a**(1/3))\n\n    # Apply the original sign back to the calculated root.\n    potential_cube_root = sign * root\n\n    # Verify if cubing this potential_cube_root yields the original number.\n    return potential_cube_root * potential_cube_root * potential_cube_root == original_a", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/76": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/76", "solution": "import math\ndef is_simple_power(x, n):\n    \"\"\"Your task is to write a function that returns true if a number x is a simple\n    power of n and false in other cases.\n    x is a simple power of n if n**int=x\n    For example:\n    is_simple_power(1, 4) => true\n    is_simple_power(2, 2) => true\n    is_simple_power(8, 2) => true\n    is_simple_power(3, 2) => false\n    is_simple_power(3, 1) => false\n    is_simple_power(5, 3) => false\n    \"\"\"\n    epsilon = 1e-9\n\n    if n == 1:\n        return x == 1\n    \n    # Handle n == 0 case carefully.\n    # 0^positive_int = 0\n    # 0^0 is often undefined, but in context of x is simple power, it might be interpreted as 1.\n    # If x is 0, it must be 0^positive_int. If x is 1, it must be 0^0.\n    if n == 0:\n        return x == 0 or x == 1\n    \n    # Any number (except